ses only when started from one cwd (the source-reading row) if CI's own invocation is green. *Note / Condition:* the source-reading row going red on a pure refactor of the line (qR: the cost of R4, which the design ruling accepted only because R4 can fail under PM); the three new `node:` imports (named by the builder as row support); the head commit's author and committer hosts (`localdomain`) and the Sonnet trailer and unsigned commit (replaced by the squash); the builder's plants run on copies before the commit existed (its Corrections: effect nil if the committed blobs equal the plant-run copies, which you cannot re-check: say so); a plant red outside the new describe (name it; not a finding); hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN (no PR: Condition, written on the line above the verdict). Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Major: quote the plant, the row and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs C1-C5 measured with their controls and zero findings above Note; GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only ("NO PR; hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN" is always such a Condition here); **NO GO on any Blocker or Major = NO GO round 1 of 2 on class "remediation register tests and titles"**: each finding with its fix-shape in prose (a forward commit on the same branch; a new head is round 2 of 2 = the cap). A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP: say it is tier-1 and unresolved.
**First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0 `GATE VERDICT B1178: PENDING`; verdict form, ONE line):** `GATE VERDICT B1178: branch b1175/hpsmpoc-437-order-pin-and-titles <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 212fbda on main <sha7> (round 1 of 2 on class "remediation register tests and titles"; NO GO 0 before; NO PR, hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN - delta <1 commit on 2a77098 y, 0 behind y, 3 paths +39 -7 y> - product file <one hunk y; git diff -w empty y; emitted JS equal y; literals n=n y; checkEntry outputs equal over n entries y> - test lines <timers/skip/only 0 y; auth-shaped added 0 y; ASCII y; names/ids 0 y> - pin <qA n red; qV n; qS n; qE n; qZ n; q0, qC, qP 0> - evidence refusal absent <qX n real-date red, date rows green y; qXs n; qXv n; qU n; qXm n> - sentence <qM n; qMf n; qD n; qR n (source row only y)> - renames <blocks 7=7 6=6 same last segments y; vanished 13 reappear y; added 11 y; consumers 0 y> - suite <head p/f/s files vs base; lint typecheck build shards audits rc; e2e NOT RUN> - message true n of N - overlap <open PRs 0; live hits n> - gitleaks rc <n> - landing files 4 checked y)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start, mid, verdict), instrument and load, PRIOR WORK, the hashed predictions with their sha256 and clocks, C1-C6 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, the blob-equality output with its controls, the hunk table, the product-file meaning table (three instruments), the plant table (plant, anchor count, landed y/n, rows red BY NAME, NEW/OLD, message), the survivor behaviour proofs, the rename census, the consumer search, the names table, the claims table, the commit-sentence table, findings `B1178-n` each with severity, class, rule applied, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class (MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY / CARRIED), the closure lines for Items 1 and 2, FOR TUESDAY, FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, trees and ports left, **UNMEASURED last** (at least: hosted CI and CodeQL (no PR); the screen in a browser and its rendered sentences (no screen-level row exists; the rows are unit rows); Linux runner fonts and Node; SQL Server (not involved); the builder's own plant counts re-made only in shape; e2e). **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B1178 branch b1175/hpsmpoc-437-order-pin-and-titles @ 212fbda <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main <sha7>` (main by `gh api -X GET` at the verdict; finding ids with severities, the class and "NO PR; hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN" on the line above it; the line carries none of the words that name a landing), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
**STATUS-NOW (binding).** At Step 0, before any heavy work, write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-03_B1178_STATUS.md`: the placeholder FIRST line, Step 0 (sha256s of source and copy, stamp-slot count with control, the `brief_seat: model=...` line if visible, the pane name via `tmux display -p -t "$TMUX_PANE" '#{@cockpit_name}'`), REFUSE counts, PINS, the ROUND COUNT text, target and hard-stop clocks absolute, one line per check C1-C6 with its evidence path. **Never start a line with `VERDICT:`, `STOPPED:` or `READY` until you mean it: Tuesday's watcher reads only the file's last line.** The LAST LINE while you work is `WORKING: <check and what is running, with a figure that moves>`; update after every check and every plant. Evidence in `Briefs/2026-11-03_B1178_evidence/` (summaries, tables, run logs, the four landing files; no secrets, no person's name). **RESUME at about 80 percent of your context or at the hard stop:** write `## PROGRESS and RESUME` (each check done/partial/not started, the next exact commands, every plant with its restore proof, processes), stop every process of yours, restore every plant, release the lock, end the FILE with `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME`. A verdict from a gate that did not finish C1, C2's qA, qV, qS, qX, qXs, qXv and qM, and C3 is conditional (add ` (conditional: <reason>)` to the first and last line).

